{"schema_version": 2, "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-terra", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 16381, "k": 8, "gap": 2, "decoy_groups": 8, "replay_span": 800000}, "seed": 1534843913, "solved": "failed", "parsed": false, "verify_ok": null, "verify_reason": "parse_answer returned None", "reply": "No such set of 8 arcs exists.\n\nAfter cancelling the batch pairs modulo 16381, the final tournament has 12 distinct reversed fixed-gap chords, at starting positions\n\n\\[\n3252,12920,9875,9703,13122,10123,8435,4480,15597,8402,7665,11172.\n\\]\n\nFor each such position \\(r\\), the final arc from position \\(r+2\\) to position \\(r\\) forms a directed triangle with the unchanged arcs from \\(r\\) to \\(r+1\\) and from \\(r+1\\) to \\(r+2\\). Since the only fixed-gap chord in that triangle is the reversed arc itself, every one of these 12 arcs must be deleted by any feedback arc set restricted to fixed-gap chords.\n\nTherefore any such feedback arc set has size at least 12, not 8.", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 85.25, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "escalated", "escalation_round": 3}
