{"schema_version": 2, "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-terra", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 16381, "k": 8, "gap": 2, "decoy_groups": 8, "replay_span": 800000}, "seed": 581661747, "solved": "failed", "parsed": false, "verify_ok": null, "verify_reason": "parse_answer returned None", "reply": "No such list of \\(K=8\\) arcs exists.\n\nAfter cancelling the paired batches modulo 2, the final tournament has 12 reversed non-wrapping fixed-gap chords, with starting positions\n\n\\[\n[392,520,535,1230,1975,4804,6519,13036,14564,14609,15717,16163].\n\\]\n\nFor every such position \\(r\\), the final tournament contains the directed triangle\n\n\\[\nr \\to r+1 \\to r+2 \\to r.\n\\]\n\nThe only fixed-gap chord in that triangle is \\(r+2\\to r\\). Therefore any feedback arc set restricted to fixed-gap chords must delete each of these 12 distinct arcs. Hence its size is at least 12, so deleting exactly 8 such arcs cannot make the final digraph acyclic.", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 105.58, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "escalated", "escalation_round": 3}
