{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 65521, "k": 8, "gap": 2, "decoy_groups": 8, "replay_span": 3200000}, "seed": 1481504918, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "[39179,24448] is not a directed arc of the final tournament", "reply": "To find the feedback arc set of size $K=8$, we analyze the effects of the 48 batches of arc reversals. \n\nAll 48 batches pair up into 24 pairs, where each pair is an arithmetic progression differing by exactly one element. Evaluating the single remaining element $x$ from each of the 24 pairs modulo $n = 65521$, we find that 16 of these residues cancel out in pairs (since each arc reversal is an involution, reversing an arc twice restores its original direction). \n\nThis leaves exactly 8 distinct values of $r = x \\bmod n$ that are reversed an odd number of times:\n$$r \\in \\{7253, 22035, 34883, 37961, 38322, 46124, 59772, 62776\\}$$\n\nIn the initial tournament, the ordering of vertices by their positions $0, 1, \\dots, n-1$ is a topological order: for any $p < q$, the arc is directed $p \\to q$. Since every $r \\le n-3$, reversing the arc between position $r$ and $(r+2)$ creates a backward arc from position $r+2$ to position $r$. Deleting these 8 backward arcs restores acyclicity.\n\nThus, each arc in the final tournament has:\n- $\\text{tail} = v(r+2)$\n- $\\text{head} = v(r)$\n\nwhere the vertex at position $p$ is given by $v(p) = (40126 \\cdot p + 30225) \\bmod n$.\n\nComputing the endpoints $[v(r+2), v(r)]$ for each of the 8 values of $r$:\n1. $r = 7253 \\implies [34552, 19821]$\n2. $r = 22035 \\implies [15471, 740]$\n3. $r = 34883 \\implies [35091, 20360]$\n4. $r = 37961 \\implies [35834, 21103]$\n5. $r = 38322 \\implies [39179, 24448]$\n6. $r = 46124 \\implies [44893, 30162]$\n7. $r = 59772 \\implies [60023, 45292]$\n8. $r = 62776 \\implies [39887, 25156]$\n\nSorting these arcs lexicographically:\n1. $[15471, 740]$\n2. $[34552, 19821]$\n3. $[35091, 20360]$\n4. $[35834, 21103]$\n5. $[39179, 24448]$\n6. $[39887, 25156]$\n7. $[44893, 30162]$\n8. $[60023, 45292]$\n\n<answer>[[15471,740],[34552,19821],[35091,20360],[35834,21103],[39179,24448],[39887,25156],[44893,30162],[60023,45292]]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 146.34, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "escalated", "escalation_round": 5}
